# API and Database Standards

## RESTful API Design
- Use consistent URL patterns: `/api/resource`
- Follow HTTP method conventions (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes
- Use consistent response formats with proper error messages
- Implement API versioning from the start
- Document all endpoints with OpenAPI/Swagger

## Request/Response Patterns
```typescript
// Standard API response format
interface ApiResponse<T> {
  success: boolean;
  data?: T;
  error?: string;
  message?: string;
}
```

## Database Design Principles
- Use meaningful table and column names
- Implement proper indexing for query performance
- Use foreign key constraints for data integrity
- Follow normalization principles
- Include audit fields (created_at, updated_at, created_by)

## Data Validation
- Validate input at API boundaries
- Use schema validation libraries (Joi, Yup, Zod)
- Implement proper sanitization for user inputs
- Validate file uploads (type, size, content)
- Use database constraints for data integrity

## Authentication & Authorization
- Implement JWT tokens for stateless authentication
- Use role-based access control (RBAC)
- Secure sensitive endpoints with proper middleware
- Implement rate limiting for API protection
- Log authentication attempts and failures

## Grading System Specific
- Store assignments with rubrics and criteria
- Track submission history and versions
- Implement grade calculation algorithms
- Store AI model responses and confidence scores
- Enable manual grade overrides with audit trails

## Error Handling
- Use consistent error response formats
- Log errors with proper context and stack traces
- Implement graceful degradation for AI service failures
- Return user-friendly error messages
- Set up proper monitoring and alerting